{%- doc -%}
  Resolves an icon to the asset that draws it.

  The kit's components take `icon` as an asset name — `wheat-slash`, `info-circle`
  — which is what a theme-editor `select` stores while showing the merchant
  "Gluten free". A merchant filling a metaobject in the admin has no select doing
  that for them: Shopify's choice list shows the very string it saves, so there
  the option has to be the readable name and the asset has to be found from it.

  Hence one resolver, taking either, and handing back the filename with the
  `icon-ui-` prefix and the `.svg` extension in place. It also absorbs the
  prefix-and-extension dance that ui-tag, ui-icon-label and ui-panel each used to
  carry a copy of.

  A readable name resolves by lowercasing and hyphenating — `Birthday cake` gives
  `birthday-cake` — and the table below carries only the ones where that lands on
  no file. **Every alias key is a name no asset has**, which is the rule that
  keeps this safe: `star` is not in the table and never can be, because
  `icon-ui-star.svg` exists and aliasing it would quietly hand a caller a
  different glyph than the one it named. That is why the option for `rating-star`
  reads "Rating star" and not "Star".

  @param {string} [name] - An asset name or a readable one. Blank and `none` give nothing.

  @example
  {%- capture icon_asset -%}{% render 'ui-icon-name', name: block.settings.icon %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign asset = ''
  assign key = name | strip | downcase

  unless key == blank or key == 'none'
    assign asset = key | replace: ' ', '-'

    assign alias_names = 'gluten-free,hand-and-heart,shipping,information,birthday-cake,baby,heart' | split: ','
    assign alias_assets = 'wheat-slash,hand-holding-heart,shipping-fast,info-circle,cake-birthday,smiling-baby,wishlist' | split: ','

    for alias in alias_names
      if alias == asset
        assign asset = alias_assets[forloop.index0]
        break
      endif
    endfor

    unless asset contains 'icon-ui-'
      assign asset = 'icon-ui-' | append: asset
    endunless
    unless asset contains '.svg'
      assign asset = asset | append: '.svg'
    endunless
  endunless
-%}
{{- asset -}}
